---
title: The site
description: What the documentation build produces besides the pages.
---

`pnpm build` in `docs/` writes the site to `docs/dist/`, and alongside it the
same documentation in the form an agent reads:

| File | What it is |
| --- | --- |
| `/llms.txt` | An index: what {{ title }} is, and a link to every page |
| `/llms-full.txt` | Every page in one document |
| `/<page>.md` | Each page as plain Markdown, beside its HTML |

All three are generated from the pages at build time, so they cannot describe
a version of the docs that has moved on. A page that renders a component the
generator has no rule for fails the build and names the component, rather
than shipping a Markdown twin with a hole in it.

## The address

The site's address is set once, at the top of `astro.config.mjs`. The build
accepts one of two layouts, never a mix:

- **A github.io project site** - `https://owner.github.io/repo/`, with the
  repository's name as the base path and no `public/CNAME`.
- **A custom domain** - `https://docs.example.com/`, served from the root,
  with `public/CNAME` holding that domain.

Every link inside the pages must start with the base path. The build lists
each one that does not.

## Publishing

`.github/workflows/docs.yml` builds and deploys the site on every push to
`main` that touches `docs/`. Turn it on once, in the repository's
**Settings -> Pages -> Source: GitHub Actions**.
